{"headword":"בָּחַן","parent_lexicon":"BDB Dictionary","content":{"senses":[{"definition":"<strong>vb. examine, try (</strong>cf. Aramaic <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּחַן</span>, Syriac <span dir=\"rtl\">ܒܰܚܶܢ</span>, <em>try, examine;</em> Arabic <span dir=\"rtl\">محن</span> i. viiii. <em>test</em>, cf. W<sup>SG 65</sup><strong>)</strong>—"},{"senses":[{"definition":"Pf. sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּחָנַ֫נִי</span> <a data-ref=\"Job 23:10\" href=\"/Job.23.10\">Jb 23:10</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">בָּחַנְתָּ</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 17:3\" href=\"/Psalms.17.3\">ψ 17:3</a> + 7 times; Impf. <span dir=\"rtl\">יִבְחָ֑ן</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 11:5\" href=\"/Psalms.11.5\">ψ 11:5</a> + 5 times; Imv. sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּחָנֵנִי</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 26:2\" href=\"/Psalms.26.2\">ψ 26:2</a> + 2 times; Inf. <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּחֹן</span> <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 13:9\" href=\"/Zechariah.13.9\">Zc 13:9</a>; Pt. <span dir=\"rtl\">בֹּחֵן</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 11:20\" href=\"/Jeremiah.11.20\">Je 11:20</a> + 5 times (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">צרף</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">נסה</span>);—"},{"senses":[{"definition":"<em>examine, scrutinize, try</em> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 11:5\" href=\"/Psalms.11.5\">ψ 11:5</a>; <a data-ref=\"Psalms 139:23\" href=\"/Psalms.139.23\">139:23</a> <a data-ref=\"Job 7:18\" href=\"/Job.7.18\">Jb 7:18</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">עַפְעַפָּיו יִבְחֲנוּ בְנֵי אָדָם</span> <em>His eyelids try the children of men</em> (search them through and through) <a data-ref=\"Psalms 11:4\" href=\"/Psalms.11.4\">ψ 11:4</a>."}],"num":"1."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<em>prove, test, try</em>."},{"senses":[{"definition":"with the metaphor of gold <a data-ref=\"Job 23:10\" href=\"/Job.23.10\">Jb 23:10</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">וּבְחַנְתִּים כִּבְחֹן אֶת־הַזָּהָב</span> <em>and I will try them as one tries gold</em> <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 13:9\" href=\"/Zechariah.13.9\">Zc 13:9</a>."}],"num":"a."},{"senses":[{"definition":"without metaphor, of God testing persons <a data-ref=\"Psalms 26:2\" href=\"/Psalms.26.2\">ψ 26:2</a>; <a data-ref=\"Psalms 66:10\" href=\"/Psalms.66.10\">66:10</a>; <a data-ref=\"Psalms 81:8\" href=\"/Psalms.81.8\">81:8</a> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 9:6\" href=\"/Jeremiah.9.6\">Je 9:6</a>; ways <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 6:27\" href=\"/Jeremiah.6.27\">Je 6:27</a> (prophet); the <span dir=\"rtl\">לֵב</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 17:3\" href=\"/Psalms.17.3\">ψ 17:3</a> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 12:3\" href=\"/Jeremiah.12.3\">Je 12:3</a> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 17:3\" href=\"/Proverbs.17.3\">Pr 17:3</a> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 29:17\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.29.17\">1 Ch 29:17</a>; reins <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 17:10\" href=\"/Jeremiah.17.10\">Je 17:10</a>; heart and reins <a data-ref=\"Psalms 7:10\" href=\"/Psalms.7.10\">ψ 7:10</a> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 11:20\" href=\"/Jeremiah.11.20\">Je 11:20</a> (= <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 20:12\" href=\"/Jeremiah.20.12\">20:12</a>)."}],"num":"b."},{"senses":[{"definition":"of man testing or tempting God <a data-ref=\"Psalms 95:9\" href=\"/Psalms.95.9\">ψ 95:9</a> <a data-ref=\"Malachi 3:10\" href=\"/Malachi.3.10\">Mal 3:10</a>, <a data-ref=\"Malachi 3:15\" href=\"/Malachi.3.15\">15</a>."}],"num":"c."},{"senses":[{"definition":"the ear trying words <a data-ref=\"Job 12:11\" href=\"/Job.12.11\">Jb 12:11</a> = <a data-ref=\"Job 34:3\" href=\"/Job.34.3\">34:3</a>."}],"num":"d."}],"num":"2."}],"form":"Qal"},{"senses":[{"definition":"Impf. <span dir=\"rtl\">יִבָּחֵן</span> <a data-ref=\"Job 34:36\" href=\"/Job.34.36\">Jb 34:36</a> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 42:15\" href=\"/Genesis.42.15\">Gn 42:15</a>, <a data-ref=\"Genesis 42:16\" href=\"/Genesis.42.16\">16</a>, <em>to be tried, proved</em>."}],"form":"Niph."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<span dir=\"rtl\">בֹּחַן</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 21:18\" href=\"/Ezekiel.21.18\">Ez 21:18</a> <em>the trial has been made</em> (𝔊 𝔖 𝔙 Ges MV Ew Ke, but noun <span dir=\"rtl\">בֹּ֫חַן</span> MT Symm Haev; read <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּחֵן</span> <em>with grace, favour</em>, Hi Co)."}],"form":"Pu."}]},"rid":"BDB01116","strong_numbers":["974"],"next_hw":"בֹּ֫חַן","prev_hw":"בָּחֵל²","all_cited":true,"brackets":"first_word","root":true,"quotes":[],"GK":["1043"],"TWOT":["230"],"parent_lexicon_details":{"name":"BDB Dictionary","language":"heb.biblical","to_language":"eng","text_categories":[],"source":"BDB Dictionary","attribution":"F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs","index_title":"BDB","version_title":"A Hebrew and English lexicon of the Old Testament, by Francis Brown. With the co-operation of S. R. Driver and Charles A. Briggs. Oxford, 1906","version_lang":"en","should_autocomplete":true}}